# Kee — User Context

> **Template.** Copy to `vault/config/user.md` and customise. Anything you
> write here is loaded into Kee's system prompt on every turn — keep it
> tight, skip secrets.

## Identity
- Name / handle
- Age, role, location (high-level — full address NOT needed)
- Primary occupation / studies

## Active Projects
- Bullet list of what you're currently working on. Used by the auto-
  dispatch hook in `agent.process()` — mention these in your messages
  and Kee will leave breadcrumbs in `dispatch_registry`.

## Technical Stack
- Languages, frameworks, infra you actually use day-to-day. Helps the
  agent pick relevant tooling.

## Communication Preferences
- Tone (direct / formal / playful)
- Default response language
- Things to avoid (filler, emojis, follow-up offers)
- Things you appreciate (challenge my reasoning, push back, etc.)

## Contact
- ⚠️ **Do not put phone numbers, real email, or private handles here**
  if you intend to make this vault public. Kee uses these only when you
  ask for an outbound message; if you do, set them via env vars instead
  (see `.env.example`).
